WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.510
Thirty students.

2
00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:04.460
Three hundred and
sixty-five days in the year.

3
00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:07.320
Each student drops a
pin on their birthday.

4
00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:12.250
With so many empty days, surely
nobody lands on someone else's day?

5
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:16.750
The model: all three hundred and
sixty-five days are equally likely,

6
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.930
ignoring the twenty-ninth
of February and twins.

7
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:23.530
So what is the chance that at
least two of them share a birthday?

8
00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.820
Under ten per cent?

9
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.310
About a half?

10
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.630
In this mission, you'll
meet the complement,

11
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:33.410
not A, whose probability is
one minus the probability of A.

12
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.120
And you'll multiply along
tree diagram branches,

13
00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:40.730
where, without replacement, the
second-stage probabilities change.

14
00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:46.210
Your mission: find how likely it is that
two of the thirty students share a birthday.
